WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:03.720
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:04.706 --> 00:00:10.482
<v><b>A:</b></v> The busiest street in the country is Madero Avenue, in Mexico City.

00:00:10.889 --> 00:00:17.411
Up to 500,000 people a day walk along this street in the capital of Mexico.

00:00:19.431 --> 00:00:20.093
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:26.506
<v><b>B:</b></v> The biggest train station in the world is Grand Central Terminal in New York.

00:00:26.982 --> 00:00:31.701
It has 44 platforms and covers nearly 2 million square feet.

00:00:33.729 --> 00:00:34.396
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:40.543
<v><b>A:</b></v> The widest bridge in the country is the Port Mann Bridge, near Vancouver.

00:00:41.098 --> 00:00:48.525
This Canadian bridge is 213 feet wide – wide enough for ten lanes of traffic.

00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:51.331
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:57.713
<v><b>B:</b></v> The tallest building in the world is Burj Khalifa in the United Arab Emirates.

00:00:58.265 --> 00:01:02.418
It is 2,716.5 feet tall.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.306
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:01:06.248 --> 00:01:09.312
<v><b>A:</b></v> The longest river in the world is the Nile.

00:01:09.592 --> 00:01:16.599
It’s 4,258 miles long and goes through eleven different African countries.

00:01:18.589 --> 00:01:19.416
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:01:20.404 --> 00:01:26.096
<v><b>B:</b></v> The most dangerous road in the world is Bayburt D915 in Türkiye.

00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:32.363
The 65-mile road is very high up and the weather is often foggy and rainy.

00:01:33.036 --> 00:01:37.037
Even really good drivers find driving extremely difficult.